@startuml session-sequence
title P2P Sync — Full Sync Session ("Sync now")

skinparam shadowing false

participant "Client C\n(dialing device)" as C
participant "Server S\n(listening device)" as S

== Authentication (plaintext messages) ==

C -> S : hello { v: 1, device_id, nonce_c }
alt peer known
  S -> C : challenge { device_id, nonce_s }
else peer unknown / unpaired
  S -> C : error { unknown_peer }
  note right : UI prompts to re-pair
end
C -> S : auth { mac = HMAC(K, "auth-c" || nonce_c || nonce_s) }
S -> C : auth_ok { mac = HMAC(K, "auth-s" || nonce_s || nonce_c) }

note over C, S
  Both derive session keys: HKDF(K, nonce_c || nonce_s)
  -> one AES-256-GCM key per direction, counter nonces.
  Every following frame: [8B counter | GCM ciphertext].
  Fresh nonces kill cross-session replay; strictly
  increasing counters kill in-session replay.
end note

== Pull phase (C pulls from S) ==

C -> S : sync_begin { cursor = applied_through_seq[S] }
S -> S : snapshot = MAX(seq) of own change log\ncollect rows with cursor < seq <= snapshot
S -> C : changes { table: 'books', rows: [...] }
S -> C : changes { table: 'ledgers', rows: [...] }
S -> C : changes { table: 'entries', rows: [...] }
note right of S : batches of <= 500 rows,\nstrictly books -> ledgers -> entries\n(ledger rows travel without balance)
S -> C : changes_done { through_seq = snapshot }
C -> C : apply batches (merge pipeline, section 6)\npersist cursor = through_seq\nin the SAME transaction as the final batch
C -> S : apply_ack { through_seq }

== Push phase (roles swap: S pulls from C) ==

S -> C : sync_begin { cursor = applied_through_seq[C] }
C -> S : changes { ... }
C -> S : changes_done { through_seq }
S -> S : apply + persist cursor
S -> C : apply_ack { through_seq }

C -> S : sync_complete
C -> S : close

== Disconnect / resume ==

alt connection drops at ANY point
  note over C, S
    Nothing to undo. Cursors advanced only where a full
    apply committed. Next session re-sends the same delta;
    re-applying is idempotent (a row whose version_hlc is
    not strictly greater than the local one is a no-op).
    Writes made during the session sit above `snapshot`
    and simply go out next time.
  end note
end

@enduml
